course: dictionary
lesson: 5988
title: Mealworm in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A mealworm is the young form, or larva, of a darkling beetle. It looks like a small yellow-brown worm, but it is not a real worm. Its clues come from the words around it.
explain: «Dried mealworms» and «mealworm beetle» show the word can mean food or a stage in a beetle's life. Read the words around it to decide which meaning fits.
explain: «A box of sand with hidden mealworms» gives clues in hidden and dig. Meerkats dig for food, so mealworms here are food the meerkats find.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. A tray of sand with food hidden for meerkats to dig still makes sense, so the meaning is right.
fact: «Mealworm» is a noun, and its plural is «mealworms».
fact: A mealworm is the larva of a darkling beetle, a small yellow-brown grub that eats grain and flour.
fact: «Mealworms» can also mean food sold for birds, reptiles and pets.
fact: In science lessons, mealworms show a life cycle: larva, pupa, then beetle.
fact: Mealworms are not real worms, even though they look like small worms.
exercise: «Meerkats dig all day in the wild, so a box of sand with hidden mealworms lets them do what they feel driven to do.» In this sentence, what are the mealworms? | Plants that grow in sand | *Food hidden for the meerkats to find | Sand toys for children | Birds that sing in the morning
exercise: According to the dictionary, what does a mealworm look like? | A big green frog | A black spider | *A small yellow-brown worm | A red flower
exercise: «Many zoos breed their own crickets and mealworms, and dust them with vitamin and calcium powder before feeding them to frogs and lizards.» What do the zoos do to the mealworms before feeding them? | Put them in a sandpit | *Dust them with vitamin and calcium powder | Cook them in a pan | Paint them green
test: What is the young form of a darkling beetle called? | Ladybird | *Mealworm | Caterpillar | Woodlouse
test: Why do zoos dust mealworms with vitamin powder? | *Because insects alone do not have enough of what frogs and lizards need | To make them change colour | To make them fly | To make them sweeter
exam: Bird lovers put mealworms out for robins. What does this tell you about mealworms? | *They are sold or put out as bird food | They only live in the sea | They are tiny metal toys | They can fly like bees
